cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "Model Mapper: what the neurons of Qwen3-8B do - a test of 'Neural Networks Are Already Clean' and a queryable neuron/concept ledger"
abstract: >-
  Model Mapper maps what the individual MLP neurons (and attention heads) of an open-weights language model do. Its
  first use was an independent test of Nick Cammarata's essay "Neural Networks Are Already Clean" on Qwen3-8B (with a
  Qwen3-0.6B comparison): concept recall depends on a handful of neurons, concepts share readable parts, and about half
  of neurons verifiably do one job. Later work (17-18 Oct 2026, exploratory) mapped 5,000 Wikipedia Vital Articles
  concepts, graded what each layer band's neurons do, and built a lossless, queryable ledger of every measurement with a
  format for third-party contributions. Several runs were still in progress at this snapshot.
